		<div class="container">
			<div class="row">
				<div class="col-12 col-md-5 col-lg-4">

					<div class="content-list-container">
													<div class="item animate" data-index="0">
								
																	<picture class="" alt=""><source media="(min-width: 768px)" srcset="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7303/easset_upload_file2464_83898_e-898x600-f50_50.jpg 1.000x,https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7303/easset_upload_file2464_83898_e-1500x1002-f50_50.jpg 1.670x"><source media="(min-width: 0px)" loading="lazy" srcset="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7303/easset_upload_file2464_83898_e-340x240-f50_50.jpg 1.000x,https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7303/easset_upload_file2464_83898_e-680x480-f50_50.jpg 2.000x"><img decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7303/easset_upload_file2464_83898_e-340x240-f50_50.jpg" srcset="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7303/easset_upload_file2464_83898_e-340x240-f50_50.jpg 1.000x,https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7303/easset_upload_file2464_83898_e-680x480-f50_50.jpg 2.000x" alt="easset_upload_file2464_83898_e" width="898" height="600" class=""></picture>																								<div class="item-content">
																			<h2 class="heading" >WALL OF HONOR</h2>																												<div class="content-container"><p>Visitors to our global headquarters in New York enter the newsroom by passing the Wall of Honor — a memorial to the 37 AP journalists who have died on assignment since we were founded in 1846.</p>
<p>Our journalists routinely cover perilous situations, from the war in Afghanistan to the front lines of the Ebola outbreak, putting themselves in danger on a daily basis to tell the world&#8217;s stories. Here we remember those who lost their lives while reporting the news.</p>
</div>
																										</div>
							</div>
													<div class="item animate" data-index="1">
								
																	<picture class="" alt=""><source media="(min-width: 768px)" srcset="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7292/ap-purksjim-teaser-rt-542x362-f50_50.jpg 0.604x,https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7292/ap-purksjim-teaser-rt-542x362-f50_50.jpg 0.604x"><source media="(min-width: 0px)" loading="lazy" srcset="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7292/ap-purksjim-teaser-rt-340x240-f50_50.jpg 1.000x,https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7292/ap-purksjim-teaser-rt-542x382-f50_50.jpg 1.594x"><img decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7292/ap-purksjim-teaser-rt-340x240-f50_50.jpg" srcset="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7292/ap-purksjim-teaser-rt-340x240-f50_50.jpg 1.000x,https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7292/ap-purksjim-teaser-rt-542x382-f50_50.jpg 1.594x" alt="cover photo" width="898" height="600" class=""><div class="image-credit"><div class="image-credit-content">Birmingham, probably 1966. Associated Press reporter Jim Purks interviews (L to R) Rev. Fred Shuttlesworth, Rev. Ralph David Abernathy and Rev. Martin Luther King Jr. during their efforts to get blacks hired to the Birmingham police force. Photo provided by Jim Purks, who does not recall who took it.</div><div class="image-credit-toggle"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
				<circle cx="8.62988" cy="9.37012" r="8.2703" stroke="white" stroke-width="0.719157"/>
				<path d="M7.97046 13.1996V7.48233H8.93054V13.1996H7.97046ZM7.91113 6.20942V5.05518H8.98987V6.20942H7.91113Z" fill="white"/>
			</svg>
			</div></div></picture>																								<div class="item-content">
																			<h2 class="heading" >Our story</h2>																												<div class="content-container"><div data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">For over 175 years, we have been breaking news and covering the world’s biggest stories, always committed to the highest standards of objective, accurate journalism. We were founded as an independent news cooperative, whose members are U.S. newspaper and broadcasters, steadfast in our mission to inform the world. From delivering the news via pony express in 1846 to working in virtual reality today, we are always innovating.</div>
<div></div>
</div>
																												<a href="https://www.ap.org/about/" class="btn btn--text btn--action" target="">Read more</a>																	</div>
							</div>
											</div>

				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="image-container">
							
														<picture class="image-0 active asset" alt=""><source media="(min-width: 768px)" srcset="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7303/easset_upload_file2464_83898_e-898x600-f50_50.jpg 1.000x,https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7303/easset_upload_file2464_83898_e-1500x1002-f50_50.jpg 1.670x"><source media="(min-width: 0px)" loading="lazy" srcset="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7303/easset_upload_file2464_83898_e-340x240-f50_50.jpg 1.000x,https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7303/easset_upload_file2464_83898_e-680x480-f50_50.jpg 2.000x"><img decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7303/easset_upload_file2464_83898_e-340x240-f50_50.jpg" srcset="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7303/easset_upload_file2464_83898_e-340x240-f50_50.jpg 1.000x,https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7303/easset_upload_file2464_83898_e-680x480-f50_50.jpg 2.000x" alt="easset_upload_file2464_83898_e" width="898" height="600" class=""></picture>				
				
							
														<picture class="image-1  asset" alt=""><source media="(min-width: 768px)" srcset="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7292/ap-purksjim-teaser-rt-542x362-f50_50.jpg 0.604x,https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7292/ap-purksjim-teaser-rt-542x362-f50_50.jpg 0.604x"><source media="(min-width: 0px)" loading="lazy" srcset="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7292/ap-purksjim-teaser-rt-340x240-f50_50.jpg 1.000x,https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7292/ap-purksjim-teaser-rt-542x382-f50_50.jpg 1.594x"><img decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7292/ap-purksjim-teaser-rt-340x240-f50_50.jpg" srcset="https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7292/ap-purksjim-teaser-rt-340x240-f50_50.jpg 1.000x,https://www.ap.org/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/7292/ap-purksjim-teaser-rt-542x382-f50_50.jpg 1.594x" alt="cover photo" width="898" height="600" class=""><div class="image-credit"><div class="image-credit-content">Birmingham, probably 1966. Associated Press reporter Jim Purks interviews (L to R) Rev. Fred Shuttlesworth, Rev. Ralph David Abernathy and Rev. Martin Luther King Jr. during their efforts to get blacks hired to the Birmingham police force. Photo provided by Jim Purks, who does not recall who took it.</div><div class="image-credit-toggle"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
